      cell { text "Value" }
      cell { text "Meaning" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[Object]] }
      cell { ty (DataView) }
      cell { text "The DataView object whose buffer's byte length is loaded." }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[CachedBufferByteLength]] }
      cell { ty (sort [#"non-negative"] integer | val(~detached~)) }
      cell { text "The byte length of the object's [[ViewedArrayBuffer]] when the Record was created." }
    ]
  ]
}

table t"table-disposable-interface-required-properties" @sec-disposable-interface#0 {
  kind properties
  thead false
  vars []
  rows [
    row [
      cell { text "Property" }
      cell { text "Value" }
      cell { text "Requirements" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { expr (code "%Symbol.dispose%") }
      cell { ty (#"function object") }
      cell { text "<p>Invoking this method notifies the Disposable object that the caller does not intend to continue to use this object. This method should perform any necessary logic to perform explicit clean-up of the resource including, but not limited to, file system handles, streams, host objects, etc. When an exception is thrown from this method, it typically means that the resource could not be explicitly freed.</p>\n<p>Invoking this method more than once on the same object should avoid repeating clean-up logic against the already-disposed resource and should not throw an exception, even if an exception was thrown on the first invocation. However, this requirement is not enforced.</p>\n<p>When using a Disposable object with a `using` or `await using` declaration, the resource will be automatically disposed when the |Block| or |Module| immediately containing the declaration has been evaluated.</p>" }
    ]
  ]
}

table t"table-disposableresource-record-fields" @sec-disposableresource-records#0 {
  kind fields
  thead false
  schema ("DisposableResource Record", false)
  vars []
  rows [
    row [
      cell { text "Field Name" }
      cell { text "Value" }
      cell { text "Meaning" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[ResourceValue]] }
      cell { ty (Object | val(undefined)) }
      cell { text "The value to be disposed." }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[Kind]] }
      cell { ty (val(~sync-dispose~) | val(~async-dispose~)) }
      cell { text "Indicates whether the resource was added by a `using` declaration or DisposableStack object (~sync-dispose~) or by an `await using` declaration or AsyncDisposableStack object (~async-dispose~)." }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[DisposeMethod]] }
      cell { ty (#"function object" | val(undefined)) }
      cell { text "A function object that will be called with [[ResourceValue]] as its *this* value when the resource is disposed." }
    ]
  ]
}

table t"table-essential-internal-methods" @sec-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots#0 {
  kind internal_methods
  thead true
  vars [proto, propertyKey, propertyDesc, receiver, value]
  rows [
    row [
      cell { text "Internal Method" }
      cell { text "Description" }
      cell { text "Definitions" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[GetPrototypeOf]] () -> completion<Object | val(null)> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It determines the object that provides inherited properties for this object. A *null* value indicates that there is no such object." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[GetPrototypeOf]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[SetPrototypeOf]] (proto: Object | val(null)) -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It associates this object with another object that provides inherited properties. Passing *null* indicates that there is no object that provides inherited properties. Returns *true* indicating that the operation was completed successfully or *false* indicating that the operation was not successful." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[SetPrototypeOf]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[IsExtensible]] () -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It determines whether it is permitted to add additional properties to this object." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[IsExtensible]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[PreventExtensions]] () -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It controls whether new properties may be added to this object. Returns *true* if the operation was successful or *false* if the operation was unsuccessful." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[PreventExtensions]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[GetOwnProperty]] (propertyKey: #"property key") -> completion<#"Property Descriptor" | val(undefined)> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It returns a Property Descriptor for the own property of this object whose key is _propertyKey_, or *undefined* if no such property exists." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[GetOwnProperty]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[DefineOwnProperty]] (propertyKey: #"property key", propertyDesc: #"Property Descriptor") -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It creates or alters the own property whose key is _propertyKey_ to have the state described by _propertyDesc_. Returns *true* if the operation was successful or *false* if the property could not be created or updated." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[DefineOwnProperty]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[HasProperty]] (propertyKey: #"property key") -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It returns a Boolean indicating whether this object already has either an own or inherited property whose key is _propertyKey_." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[HasProperty]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[Get]] (propertyKey: #"property key", receiver: #"ECMAScript language value") -> completion<#"ECMAScript language value"> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It returns the value of the property whose key is _propertyKey_ from this object. If any ECMAScript code must be executed to retrieve the property value, _receiver_ is used as the *this* value when evaluating the code." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[Get]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[Set]] (propertyKey: #"property key", value: #"ECMAScript language value", receiver: #"ECMAScript language value") -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It sets the value of the property whose key is _propertyKey_ to _value_. If any ECMAScript code must be executed to set the property value, _receiver_ is used as the *this* value when evaluating the code. Returns *true* if the property value was set or *false* if it could not be set." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[Set]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[Delete]] (propertyKey: #"property key") -> completion<Boolean> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It removes the own property whose key is _propertyKey_ from this object. Returns *false* if the property was not deleted and is still present. Returns *true* if the property was deleted or is not present." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[Delete]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { sig (field [[OwnPropertyKeys]] () -> completion<list<#"property key">> | #"throw completion") }
      cell { text "It returns a List whose elements are all of the own property keys for the object." }
      cell { text "Within this specification it has definitions in the following types; hosts may provide additional types with their own definitions:\n<emu-internal-method-dfns for=\"[[OwnPropertyKeys]]\"></emu-internal-method-dfns>" }
    ]
  ]
}

