table t"table-realm-record-fields" @sec-code-realms#0 {
  kind fields
  thead true
  schema ("Realm Record", false)
  vars []
  rows [
    row [
      cell { text "Field Name" }
      cell { text "Value" }
      cell { text "Meaning" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[AgentSignifier]] }
      cell { ty (#"agent signifier") }
      cell { text "The agent that owns this realm" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[Intrinsics]] }
      cell { ty (pred(sat @ph-type-intrinsic-keys())) }
      cell { text "The intrinsic values used by code associated with this realm" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[GlobalObject]] }
      cell { ty (Object) }
      cell { text "The global object for this realm" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[GlobalEnv]] }
      cell { ty (#"Global Environment Record") }
      cell { text "The global environment for this realm" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[TemplateMap]] }
      cell { ty (records [[[Site]]: pred(sat @ph-type-nt-parse-node(data choice 0, |TemplateLiteral|)), [[Array]]: Array]) }
      cell { text "<p>Template objects are canonicalized separately for each realm using its Realm Record's [[TemplateMap]]. Each [[Site]] value is a Parse Node that is a |TemplateLiteral|. The associated [[Array]] value is the corresponding template object that is passed to a tag function.</p>\n<emu-note>Once a Parse Node becomes unreachable, the corresponding [[Array]] is also unreachable, and it would be unobservable if an implementation removed the pair from the [[TemplateMap]] list.</emu-note>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[LoadedModules]] }
      cell { ty (list<#"LoadedModuleRequest Record">) }
      cell { text "<p>A map from the specifier strings imported by this realm to the resolved Module Record. The list does not contain two different Records _r1_ and _r2_ such that ModuleRequestsEqual(_r1_, _r2_) is *true*.</p>\n<emu-note>\n  As mentioned in HostLoadImportedModule (<emu-xref href=\"#note-HostLoadImportedModule-referrer-Realm-Record\"></emu-xref>), [[LoadedModules]] in Realm Records is only used when running an `import()` expression in a context where there is no active script or module.\n</emu-note>" }
    ]
    row [
      cell { field [[HostDefined]] }
      cell { ty (pred(sat @spec-copy-6(data choice 0, undefined))) }
      cell { text "Field reserved for use by hosts that need to associate additional information with a Realm Record." }
    ]
  ]
}

table t"table-reference-record-fields" @sec-reference-record-specification-type#0 {
